# Append-only / independently-ticked files use git's union merge driver.
#
# Why: several agents work concurrently, and both of these files get touched
# by nearly every PR (checkboxes in PLAN.md, entries in DECISIONS.md).
# With the default merge driver that guarantees a conflict on every merge.
# `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides' added lines instead of conflicting, which
# is exactly the right semantics for a checklist and an append-only log.
#
# Caveat worth knowing: if two agents edit the SAME line, union keeps both
# versions of it, so you may occasionally see a duplicated line. That is
# trivially spotted and deleted, and is a far better failure mode than a
# merge conflict on every single PR.
#
# Agents may therefore tick their own PLAN.md boxes and append their own
# DECISIONS.md entries directly. No orchestrator bottleneck.

docs/PLAN.md      merge=union
docs/DECISIONS.md merge=union

# Generated protobuf code is committed but should not clutter diffs or
# count toward language stats.
proto/gen/** linguist-generated=true

# Normalise line endings so agents on different machines don't fight
* text=auto eol=lf
